<#ftl output_format="HTML" auto_esc=true>
<#-- These feature values come from the native TogglyModelAttribute @ControllerAdvice.
     The empty map is used only by the visibly unconfigured setup shell. -->
<#macro badge value><span class="badge ${value?then('on','off')}">${value?then('ON','OFF')}</span></#macro>
<#macro presets><div class="presets"><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="matching">Matching preset</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="nonmatching">Non-matching preset</button></form></div></#macro>
<#macro table keys><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag key</th><th>Definition</th><th>This request</th></tr></thead><tbody><#list keys as key><tr data-flag="${key}"><td><code>${key}</code></td><td>${definitions?seq_contains(key)?then('Present','Absent')}</td><td><@badge value=(features[key])!false/><#if key == 'filter-device-type'> <small>Macintosh detection unsupported in 1.5.1</small></#if></td></tr></#list></tbody></table></div></#macro>
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>${title} · Java Spring MVC SDK Sample</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script src="/workshop.js" defer></script></head><body>
<header><p class="eyebrow">TOGGLY / JAVA SPRING MVC</p><a class="brand" href="/">Feature flag workshop</a><p>Learn native Spring MVC, one request at a time.</p></header>
<nav aria-label="Sections"><#list paths as link><a href="${link}">${titles[link?index]}</a></#list></nav><main>
<#if !configured><aside class="warning" role="status"><strong>Missing TOGGLY_APP_KEY — unconfigured offline mode.</strong> No live evaluations or synthetic enabled flags. Protected examples deny with 503. <a href="/configuration">Set up your app</a>.</aside>
<#else><aside class="status">Signed definitions configured · ${definitions?size} current definitions · HTTP poll every 60 seconds in normal startup. Reload to see current evaluations.</aside><#if definitions?size == 0><aside class="warning">No definitions available yet. Missing flags use false defaults; check your key, environment and connection.</aside></#if></#if>
<#if errors gt 0><aside class="warning">SDK refresh errors observed: ${errors}. The SDK retains its last valid signed definitions. This cumulative warning remains after recovery; inspect current flags and retry refresh.</aside></#if>
<p class="context">User: <strong>${identity?has_content?then(identity,'anonymous')}</strong> · Order: <strong>${order}</strong> · Demo identities are not authentication.</p><h1>${title}</h1>
<#switch path>
<#case '/'>
<p>Follow the sections from a Boolean flag to isolated users, Orders and native controller gates.</p><div class="cards"><#list paths as link><#if link != '/' ><a class="card" href="${link}"><span>${link?index}</span><h2>${titles[link?index]}</h2></a></#if></#list></div>
<h2>First flag exercise</h2><ol><li>Complete Configuration and create <code>new-dashboard</code> in Production.</li><li>Enable it, wait up to 60 seconds or use Refresh in Spring MVC integration.</li><li>Open Declarative gates: the feature route allows and the negate route denies.</li><li>Disable the flag, refresh, and observe the opposite behavior.</li></ol>
<h2>Flag checklist and current snapshot</h2><p>When configured, native model advice evaluates these flags for this request before the template renders. Absent means the key is missing from current definitions, not simply OFF.</p><@table keys=flags/><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Programmatic JSON snapshot</a></p>
<#break>
<#case '/gates'>
<p>The native <code>FeatureGateInterceptor</code> reads <code>@FeatureGate</code> on controllers and methods. It runs after context setup and denies configured gates with 404 by default.</p>
<div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>Feature</h2><@badge value=(features['new-dashboard'])!false/><p><a href="/gated/feature">Try feature route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>Negate</h2><@badge value=configured && !((features['new-dashboard'])!false)/><p><a href="/gated/negate">Try negate route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ALL: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=allOn/><p><a href="/gated/all">Try ALL route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ANY: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=anyOn/><p><a href="/gated/any">Try ANY route</a></p></article></div>
<h2>Real template integration</h2>
<#-- FreeMarker branches use the actual native advice's features map, not a sample evaluator. -->
<#if (features['new-dashboard'])!false><p id="dashboard-content">New dashboard content is visible.</p><#else><p id="dashboard-content">Classic dashboard fallback is visible.</p></#if>
<p><code>TogglyModelAttribute</code> supplies <code>features</code>. This FreeMarker condition is ordinary view composition; the SDK owns the evaluation. Hiding HTML is not an access-control boundary: the native route gate checks again before the action.</p>
<h2>Variants</h2><aside class="note">Native variant allocation is unsupported in io.toggly core/MVC 1.5.1. No variant is fabricated. <code>getValue</code> selects between two caller-provided values using a Boolean flag; telemetry variant labels do not allocate experiments.</aside>
<#break>
<#case '/programmatic'>
<p>Use explicit immutable context for service code. Native <code>getValue</code> below reads the synchronous ContextHolder; it selects a Boolean branch, not a variant.</p><pre>client.isEnabled("api-v2", context)
client.gate(List.of("new-dashboard", "api-v2"),
    FeatureRequirement.ALL, false, context)
client.evaluateAll(context)
client.getValue("api-v2", "v2", "v1")</pre>
<p>Current API version: <strong>${apiVersion}</strong></p><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Open current request JSON</a> · <a href="/api/flag/unknown">Unknown flag defaults false</a></p><form method="post" action="/actions/submit"><button>Try enhanced submit</button></form><p>This method has <code>@FeatureGate(value="enhanced-submit", status=403)</code>. The native interceptor denies before the controller runs; no order is persisted. Unconfigured actions return 503.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/identity'>
<p>A session stores demo inputs, never evaluated flag results. <code>DemoContextResolver.resolve</code> constructs immutable identity, claims, request fields and Order before native gates, argument resolution or model advice.</p><@presets/>
<h2>Customize this session</h2><form class="fields" method="post" action="/context"><label>Identity<input name="identity" maxlength="512" value="${identity}"></label><label>Claim role<input name="role" maxlength="512" value="${role}"></label><label>Country<input name="country" maxlength="512" value="${country}"></label><label>Accept-Language<input name="language" maxlength="512" value="${language}"></label><label>User-Agent<input name="userAgent" maxlength="512" value="${userAgent}"></label><label>Order<select name="order"><option value="vip"<#if order == 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-vip</option><option value="standard"<#if order != 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-standard</option></select></label><button>Apply session context</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="clear">Clear session identity</button></form>
<p>Initial anonymous requests read actual User-Agent, Accept-Language and cf-ipcountry headers where present. Presets deliberately override these fields. These local controls are not trusted authentication; in a deployed app derive identity and claims from authenticated server state, and country from a trusted proxy.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/orders'>
<p>User identity stays the same while the entity changes. These checks run side by side in one request using <code>context.withEntity(...)</code>, with kind Order, Id, Vip and Total.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>ord-vip · Vip=true</h2><span id="vip-result"><@badge value=vipOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=vip">Select VIP for this request</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ord-standard · Vip=false</h2><span id="standard-result"><@badge value=standardOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=standard">Select standard for this request</a></p></article></div><p>Without an entity: <span id="missing-result"><@badge value=missingOn/></span> · <a href="/orders?order=missing">Try missing entity</a></p><pre>var order = new TogglyEntityContext("Order", "ord-vip",
    Map.of("Id", "ord-vip", "Vip", true, "Total", 250));
client.isEnabled("ExpressCheckout", context.withEntity(order));</pre><p>Never reuse a Boolean result across different Orders. The published engine compares attributes without enforcing definition.contextKind; this app explicitly constructs Order at its boundary. A missing entity evaluates false.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/filters'>
<p>All eleven rows use the native model advice and real installed SDK. Apply a saved preset or compare one request without changing your session.</p><@presets/><p><a href="/filters?preset=matching">Matching for this request</a> · <a href="/filters?preset=nonmatching">Non-matching for this request</a></p><@table keys=filters/>
<p>AlwaysOn stays ON for both; TimeWindow stays ON during 2020–2099. Percentage is sticky per identity and flag, so Alice/Bob are not prescribed ON/OFF. The seven other supported segment/context rows should be ON for Matching and OFF for Non-matching. DeviceType Macintosh is a native SDK gap: the parser recognizes iPhone/iPad/iPod but returns Other for desktop Macintosh. The exact shared rule remains OFF.</p><p>Matching: alice, role=admin, US, Chrome/en, Macintosh device, Mac OS, VIP Order. Non-matching: bob, role=user, CA, Firefox/fr, Windows, standard Order. Identity shows all exact request fields.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/mvc'>
<h2>Native pipeline</h2><ol><li>Application startup creates a native TogglyClient with its owned signed HTTP provider.</li><li>DispatcherServlet calls native <code>TogglyContextInterceptor</code>, order 0, with our <code>ContextResolver</code>.</li><li>An explicit missing-key guard denies protected examples, order 1.</li><li>Native <code>FeatureGateInterceptor</code>, order 2, checks method/class annotations.</li><li>Native <code>TogglyModelAttribute</code> computes the <code>features</code> model; native <code>FeatureArgumentResolver</code> resolves annotated Boolean parameters.</li><li>The controller returns a FreeMarker view or response.</li><li>Native <code>afterCompletion</code> clears the thread's context on allowed, denied and throwing requests.</li><li>On shutdown Tomcat stops requests and destroys Spring; then SampleRuntime closes its client and owned polling provider.</li></ol>
<p><a href="/gated/beta">Try native beta-access gate</a> · <a href="/native/argument">Try native Boolean argument</a></p><pre>@GetMapping("/native/argument")
public String argument(
    @FeatureArgumentResolver.FeatureFlag("filter-targeting") boolean enabled)</pre><form data-native-refresh method="post" action="/api/refresh"><button>Request native definitions refresh</button></form><output id="refresh-result" aria-live="polite"></output><p>This sample endpoint calls native <code>client.refresh()</code>; a completed attempt can retain the prior snapshot after an error. Return Home to inspect flags and the cumulative warning.</p>
<h2>Thread lifetime</h2><p>This app uses synchronous MVC actions and disables Servlet async. Native ContextHolder is thread-local. For executor work pass immutable EvaluationContext explicitly; do not assume it flows into another thread, Callable, DeferredResult or async dispatch.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/configuration'>
<h2>Connect your own application</h2><ol><li>Open app.toggly.io and select workspace <strong>Toggly Samples</strong>.</li><li>Create <strong>Java Spring MVC SDK Sample</strong>; select <strong>Java</strong> technology and <strong>Production</strong> environment.</li><li>Add allowed origins <code>http://localhost:8088</code> and <code>http://127.0.0.1:8088</code>.</li><li>Add Order with Id string key, Vip boolean and Total optional number.</li><li>Create all sixteen flags and the Filters category using the README recipe.</li><li>Copy .env.example to .env, set your key locally, export it, and restart.</li></ol><p>Never commit a real key. The missing-key app makes no Toggly requests and has no synthetic live data.</p><h2>Loading, refresh and errors</h2><p>Startup attempts signed definitions. Unknown flags default false. The native provider can fetch again on empty snapshots, polls every 60 seconds and retains last valid definitions after network or signature failures. Pages reevaluate the current context; results are never stored in sessions. Initial unavailable definitions show a warning rather than claiming live OFF is confirmed.</p><p>Tests use the real HTTP provider against isolated signed loopback definitions with temporary cryptographic keys. Those fixtures are not in the production package. Live dashboard setup has not been verified.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/allowed'><p>The published FeatureGateInterceptor allowed this request before the controller ran.</p><@table keys=flags/><#break>
</#switch>
</main><footer>Published io.toggly 1.5.1 · Spring MVC 7.0.9 · FreeMarker 2.3.35 · Tomcat 11 · Java 26</footer></body></html>
